## PART C — NEW WORKFLOWS TO IMPLEMENT

### C1. Approval Chain Engine
A unified approval system:
- Any user action that triggers an approval rule (defined in Settings) creates an Approval Request
- Routed to the configured role (Operations/Finance/Admin)
- Appears in that role's Approval Queue widget on Command Center
- Approver sees context, can approve/reject with reason
- Original user is notified of outcome
- All approval decisions appear in Audit Log

Rules to pre-configure:
- Quote discount > 10% → Finance approval
- Quote discount > 25% → Admin approval
- DO release with unpaid invoice → Finance approval
- Credit limit increase → Admin approval
- Invoice write-off > ₹25,000 → Finance approval
- Invoice write-off > ₹1,00,000 → Admin approval
- Agent payment > ₹5,00,000 → Admin approval
- Rate override on booking (below cost) → Admin approval

### C2. Rolling Cargo / Short-Shipped Handling
When cargo booked for a vessel does not load (missed cutoff, no space, documentation delay):
- "Mark as Rolled" button on shipment
- Prompts: Reason (no space / cutoff missed / documentation / port congestion / customer request), New Vessel (dropdown of next sailings on same lane), New ETD/ETA, Customer notification required (auto-send WhatsApp)
- Timeline event logged
- If rolled > 2 times, auto-flag for Operations review

### C3. Letter of Credit (LC) Workflow
For LC-based exports:
- LC tab on shipment: LC number, issuing bank, advising bank, latest shipment date, LC expiry, beneficiary bank
- Document checklist per LC terms (which docs are mandatory in bank set)
- "Prepare Bank Set" action: generates PDF package of HBL (3 originals), commercial invoice, packing list, insurance, certificate of origin, phytosanitary, inspection cert, SDF, bill of exchange, as applicable
- Flag discrepancies before dispatch (e.g., HBL date later than latest shipment date = DISCREPANCY)
- Track bank set dispatch (courier, AWB), bank acknowledgment, payment realization

### C4. Marine Insurance Module
- Policy types: Open policy (annual), Specific policy (per shipment), Declared value coverage
- Per-shipment: Insured value, premium, policy number, insurer, cover type (ICC A/B/C)
- Auto-generate Marine Cover Note
- Claims module: Loss event logging, surveyor assignment, claim submission tracker

### C5. Advanced Filings (Country-Specific Pre-Arrival)
A shipment destined to:
- USA → ISF 10+2 filing (24 hours before loading at POL)
- EU → ENS filing (24 hours before loading)
- Japan → AFR filing (24 hours before loading)
- China → CSD-ADV filing
System detects POD country, surfaces required filing in the shipment's Filings tab, with deadline countdown and status.

